{
  "text": " Extraordinary injustice demands extraordinary lawyers. And now we are winning. Build upon the groundbreaking COVID litigation conference in Atlanta and join the lawyers at the forefront of this growing field. As cases are being won and damages awarded, a recent poll suggests over 40% of Americans would be party to a COVID class action lawsuit. Experts predict COVID litigation will surpass the combined impact of big tobacco and asbestos cases. We invite attorneys to join this important opportunity at the second COVID litigation conference coming to Las Vegas March 7th and 8th, 2024. Connect with a diverse group of attorneys for strategic networking and expand your practice in the COVID space. Having a network of people to fall back on who actually understand what it is they're talking about has been critical for me. Learn from the leaders at the frontier who are bringing cases. I sued Rochester General six times. I won in court each of those six times. Get exclusive resources and the insights you need to litigate COVID cases now from panels, keynotes and more. At the conference, you're going to see some of the most seasoned COVID litigation attorneys. I always learn something. Litigate with confidence and be empowered by the transformative event shaping national policy. Who will right these extraordinary wrongs? You will at the second COVID litigation conference. Register now at covidlitigation.com.",
